From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:40:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0080: deferred operations ask the driver only once
 the GPU's progress word says they are done

PopPendingOperations runs at every draw and asked the driver where the GPU
is (vkGetSemaphoreCounterValue, a system call) once every 16 draws while
the oldest pending operation was not known to be done. With the GPU
behind, as in Astro Bot's garden, that was 1.6 % of the command thread
for nothing. It now asks only when the word the GPU writes at the end of
each command buffer (0064) says that operation is done; the semaphore
still decides. Without that word, once every 16 calls as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../host_gpu/renderer/commandScheduler.cpp         | 14 ++++++++++----
 src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/masterSemaphore.h   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/commandScheduler.cpp b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/commandScheduler.cpp
index 32e4b61d..4255d9a1 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/commandScheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/commandScheduler.cpp
@@ -308,12 +308,18 @@ void CommandScheduler::Wait(uint64_t tick) {
 void CommandScheduler::PopPendingOperations() {
 	// GameFlex: this runs at every draw, and asking the driver where the GPU is costs a system call
 	// (vkGetSemaphoreCounterValue, an ioctl): 9 % of the command thread in Kingdom Hearts III. Ask only
-	// when the oldest pending operation is not already known to be done, and at most once every 16
-	// calls; these operations wait for the GPU anyway, a few draws later changes nothing.
+	// when the oldest pending operation is not already known to be done, and when the word the GPU writes
+	// at the end of each command buffer (0064) says it is: with the GPU behind, as in Astro Bot's garden,
+	// asking once every 16 draws still cost 1.6 % of the thread for nothing. The semaphore decides. Without
+	// that word, once every 16 calls; these operations wait for the GPU anyway.
 	{
 		std::lock_guard lock(m_operation_mutex);
-		if (m_pending_operations.empty() ||
-		    (!m_master.IsFree(m_pending_operations.front().tick) && (++m_refresh_skips & 15u) != 0)) {
+		if (m_pending_operations.empty()) {
+			return;
+		}
+		const auto tick = m_pending_operations.front().tick;
+		if (!m_master.IsFree(tick) && (m_master.HasProgressWord() ? m_master.Progress() < tick
+		                                                          : (++m_refresh_skips & 15u) != 0)) {
 			return;
 		}
 	}
diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/masterSemaphore.h b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/masterSemaphore.h
index 41baa5f6..a61c1463 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/masterSemaphore.h
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/masterSemaphore.h
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@ public:
 	// caches, so memory is read and resources are reused after KnownGpuTick, which the kernel signals once the
 	// caches are written back. For the decisions of the scheduler, which asking the driver cost a system call.
 	void                   SetProgressWord(const uint32_t* word) noexcept { m_progress_word = word; }
+	[[nodiscard]] bool     HasProgressWord() const noexcept { return m_progress_word != nullptr; }
 	[[nodiscard]] uint64_t Progress();
 
 private:
